  "description": "Re-derives the keystone muon(3,2)/electron(3,1,1) projected Markov shift using the keystone block weight W_lambda = d_q^2/[n]_q! instead of the SU(2) Jones-Markov weight y_lambda, which is EXACTLY ZERO on the electron block (>2 rows, by the Schur-Weyl row-count rule) and therefore made the original comparison vacuous on one side. Under W_lambda both sides are nonzero. Of the two legs of the PR #2584 refutation, the magnitude leg survives (3.35e6x too large -- a scope-(a) negative) and the bar-parity leg fails (the shift is exactly bar-EVEN). The ledger's stronger claim that the Markov-trace surface is 'exhausted' was a scope-(b) structural exclusion resting on the refuted leg. No fit; nothing wired.",
